'''''Peripeltopleurus''''' is an [[extinct]] [[genus]] of prehistoric [[ray-finned fish]] that lived during the [[Anisian]] to [[Sinemurian]] [[age (geology)|ages]] of the [[Middle Triassic]]-[[Early Jurassic]] [[epoch (geology)|epoch]].<ref name="sepkoskidb">{{cite journal | last = Sepkoski | first = Jack | title =  A compendium of fossil marine animal genera | journal = Bulletins of American Paleontology | volume = 364 |page=560 | year = 2002 | url = http://strata.ummp.lsa.umich.edu/jack/showgenera.php?taxon=611&rank=class | accessdate = 2009-02-27 }}</ref><ref name="Ostenolepis">{{Cite journal |last1=Franceschi |first1=F. |last2=Marramà |first2=G. |last3=Carnevale |first3=G. |year=2026 |title=Bony fishes (Osteichthyes) from the Sinemurian (Jurassic) Osteno Konservat-Lagerstätte (Como, NW Italy) |journal=Rivista Italiana di Paleontologia e Stratigrafia |volume=132 |issue=1 |pages=9–58 |doi=10.54103/2039-4942/29058|doi-access=free }}</ref> Represents the only known Jurassic survivor of the order Peltopleuriformes.<ref name="Ostenolepis" />

